    },
    {
      "name": "closing a tab takes its panes with it",
      "why": "Recorded, and the sharpest trap in the capture: of five panes created, one got pane_closed, one got pane_exited, and two vanished with a parent that announced only itself. A mirror that removes only what it is told about keeps rendering panes whose terminal is gone, and the user has no way to dismiss them. The cascade is the mirror's own inference rather than something the backend said, which is why the change records that it was one.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "workspaces": [
            {
              "id": "w1",
              "label": "tmp"
            }
          ],
          "tabs": [
            {
              "id": "w1:t1",
              "workspace": "w1",
              "label": "1"
            },
            {
              "id": "w1:t2",
              "workspace": "w1",
              "label": "2"
            }
          ],
          "panes": [
            {
              "id": "w1:p1",
              "tab": "w1:t1",
              "workspace": "w1",
              "agentState": "idle"
            },
            {
              "id": "w1:p4",
              "tab": "w1:t2",
              "workspace": "w1",
              "agentState": "idle"
            }
          ]
        },
        "events": [
          {
            "kind": "tabRemoved",
            "id": "w1:t2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "panes": [
          "w1:p1"
        ],
        "tabs": [
          "w1:t1"
        ],
        "workspaces": [
          "w1"
        ],
        "agentStates": {
          "w1:p1": "idle"
        },
        "focus": {},
        "health": "connected",
        "changes": [
          "paneRemoved:w1:p4:cascaded",
          "tabRemoved:w1:t2"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "closing a workspace takes its tabs and their panes",
      "why": "The same trap one level up, and also recorded: workspace_closed for w2 arrived with no tab_closed for w2:t1 and no pane_closed for w2:p1. Two levels of cascade, so a mirror that handles only the direct children still leaks the panes underneath.",
